const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文研究政治关联和国有控制如何与中国公司诉讼结果相关。 阅读时应把它理解为受样本、时点和制度限定的问题，而不是可以脱离条件的结论。",en:"The article studies how political connections and state ownership relate to corporate litigation outcomes in China. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它使用政治关联和国有控制分类比较诉讼观测，案件定义和上诉结果是实证设计的一部分。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中一项，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It compares litigation observations using political-connection and state-control classifications, with case definitions and appeal outcomes forming part of the empirical design. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"输入需要诉讼记录、原被告身份、立案与结果日期、收益或公司指标、政治关联编码、国有控制状态和法院阶段标签。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原研究分别记录，不能仅因变量同名或使用最新修订值就视为可比。",en:"Inputs need litigation-case records, plaintiff and defendant identities, filing and outcome dates, return or firm measures, political-connection coding, state-control status, and court-stage labels. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源报告历史诉讼样本中的相关性，不裁定个案的是非，也不证明当前司法、政治或公司行为。 它只支持来源所描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The source reports associations in a historical litigation sample; it does not determine the merits of any case or establish current judicial, political, or corporate conduct. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"冻结法律事件编码和结果阶段；区分公告与裁判日期；记录关联和所有权分类规则；保留案件纳入、上诉和缺失记录。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Freeze legal-event coding and outcome stage; distinguish announcement from ruling dates; document connection and ownership classification rules; retain case inclusion, appeals, and missing records. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Law and Economics (2011)。该环境不是法律意见或实时诉讼风险评级，历史相关性不能脱离完整事实套用于单个争议。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Law and Economics (2011). This empirical setting is not legal advice or a current litigation-risk rating, and historical associations cannot be applied to an individual dispute without its full facts. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1086/659261",label:{zh:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Law and Economics (2011) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Effects of Political Connections and State Ownership on Corporate Litigation in China”公开说明的研究对象与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。该环境不是法律意见或实时诉讼风险评级，历史相关性不能脱离完整事实套用于单个争议。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Effects of Political Connections and State Ownership on Corporate Litigation in China”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
